#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0487 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
#note "[STALE MECHANISM, corrected 2026-08-27] NonEmptyGuardInliner was DELETED (Fix #367 / EC-100) and no guard is injected at load any more; the expectation below still holds, but for the rule's AUTHORED Requirements/Check, not for the injection this note describes. THE 82-RULE GENERATOR-WILDCARD POPULATION (Fix #331 finding; owner ruled 2026-08-22 that all 82 are BUCKET 1 - no rule edit - with a sample of fixtures owed by the closing lane; authored by Fix #340). These rules never carried the injected var_exists guard in rules/ (NonEmptyGuardInliner.isGeneratorWildcard excludes wildcard names), but WildcardExpander re-ran installNativeExpr on the EXPANDED rule, where the arm wrapped the now-concrete leaf - so before Fix #330 an absent primary column silenced them at runtime. With the arm retired the expanded leaf is a bare empty(X): absent = all-missing, TRUE on every row. The mirror of the invalid pin: here the SECONDARY column CRIT1FN is the absent one. The y=1 tuple is raised off the declared CRIT1FL, and not empty(CRIT1FN) is FALSE on every row of an absent column, so the conjunction cannot hold and the rule is correctly silent. This is why the 82 are bucket 1 rather than bucket 2: the companion conjunct genuinely restricts, so an absent column can never flood."
dataset ADLBC class=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col CRIT1FL type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | GLUC | Y
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | GLUC |
---
